<p>YouTube shows a channel through four pictures. Each has a size, a safe area and a job, and each is a frame here.</p>
<ul>
	<li><a href="/content-creation/youtube/channel-art/">Channel art</a> — 2560 × 1440, of which every device shows only the middle 1546 × 423.</li>
	<li><a href="/content-creation/youtube/profile-art/">Profile art</a> — 800 × 800, shown as a circle at 40 pixels.</li>
	<li><a href="/content-creation/youtube/thumbnail/">The thumbnail as a cover</a> — 1280 × 720, and the one picture that decides whether a film is watched.</li>
	<li><a href="/content-creation/youtube/grid/">The grid</a> — how a set of them reads side by side, which is how they are always seen.</li>
</ul>
